## Recoverable agent execution checkpoints (AgentRewind / CCC K282)

- **Aligned checkpoint = context + environment.** Record the pair `(context, environment)` at each LLM decision boundary, not either alone. Environment rewind is the largest single component (ablation: 87.8 → 43.9 success without it) — discarded-suffix side effects otherwise persist.
- **Resume-from-checkpoint, not restart-from-zero.** Restart-with-experiences discards completed work; rewind retains the validated prefix and replaces only the failing suffix.
- **Rewind memory** — retain prior-attempt info (falsified hypotheses, alternative strategies) with the restored context, so the second attempt is informed, not blind.
- **Recovery boundary honesty** — only the workspace directory tree is reversible; network/external-service side effects are not undone and must not be re-triggered (replay the retained prefix from the log, never re-execute).
- Recovery after error propagation — not only plan refinement pre-error (pairs K239 execution fidelity, K242 rollback).
- `.local/adopts/replay-agent-recorder` (MIT) + `.local/adopts/MettleBench` (Apache-2.0) = GO REFERENCE. Framework runtime **`wont_wire`**.

## Test-time world model — validate-before-act (Twin / CCC K283)

- **Validate-before-act is a harness gate, not agent discretion.** Block every scored/env action until the twin replays the full interaction log; a mismatch is a counterexample that invalidates the twin until repair.
- **Counterexample-driven repair (CEGIS)** — a repaired twin must replay the *full* log, so a local fix can't break an earlier mechanic.
- **Goal hypothesis before first reward** — propose a tentative goal predicate (must evaluate false on every logged frame; previously-reached non-goals are permanently excluded) and test the cheapest plan; a level boundary confirms.
- **Asymmetric objective** — fit (`∀` every logged transition) is the hard precondition; reachability (`∃` one imagined route) is pursued only through search.
- Pairs K231 Tycho — don't auto-build world models every verify-fail unless advantage-gated, but when building, require replay validation before any scored action.
- `.local/adopts/TWIN-ARC-AGI-3` (MIT) = GO REFERENCE. ARC bench runtime **`wont_wire`**.

## Differential fault injection for LLM modernization (CCC K284)

